.TH LIBPFM 3  "September, 2026" "" "Linux Programmer's Manual"
.SH NAME
libpfm_arm_apple_m1 - support for Apple A14/M1 core PMU
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <perfmon/pfmlib.h>
.sp
.B PMU name: apple_m1
.B PMU desc: Apple A14/M1 Series
.sp
.SH DESCRIPTION
The library supports the Apple A14/M1 core PMU, the icestorm and firestorm variants across all SoCs.

This PMU supports 10 counters and privilege levels filtering, the chip itself is an Arm 8.4-A chip.

These events are only those derived from `/usr/share/kpep` on any macOS install. There are more that can be actually measured with hardware, but we don't have any idea what they measure.

.SH MODIFIERS
The following modifiers are supported on Apple A14/M1:
.TP
.B u
Measure at the user level. This corresponds to \fBPFM_PLM3\fR.
This is a boolean modifier.
.TP
.B k
Measure at the kernel level. This corresponds to \fBPFM_PLM0\fR.
This is a boolean modifier.
.TP
.B hv
Measure at the hypervisor level. This corresponds to \fBPFM_PLMH\fR.
This is a boolean modifier.

